senses.gloss:
unnata,
(1) adj. (ppp.; cf. prec. and next; not recorded in this evil sense), arrogant: Mv 〔i.305.15〕 uddhatāṃ unnatāṃ dṛṣṭvā capalāṃ …; Śikṣ 〔158.5〕 bodhisattvo 'n-unnatavīryo bhavati;
(2) n. of a former Buddha: LV 〔5.8〕; Mv 〔i.137.12〕 (here of course in the good sense recorded in Skt. and Pali, lofty).
